() Tj
T*
(### Generic SheetDb persistence behavior) Tj
T*
(- `id` is the effective primary key for every registered table.) Tj
T*
(- `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, and `deletedAt` are conventional system columns configured through `Config` / script properties.) Tj
T*
(- Insert behavior:) Tj
T*
(  - auto-generates `id` when missing) Tj
T*
(  - auto-populates `createdAt`) Tj
T*
(  - always refreshes `updatedAt`) Tj
T*
(  - initializes `deletedAt` to `''` when omitted) Tj
T*
(- `findAll\(\)` only returns rows where `deletedAt` is blank, confirming soft-delete behavior is active globally.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Soft-delete and audit notes) Tj
T*
(- The current codebase uses `deletedAt`, not `_rowStatus`.) Tj
T*
(- No table in this repo currently uses `_rowStatus = 'active'` filtering.) Tj
T*
(- Audit/log tables \(`audit_log`, `audit_logs`\) still include `deletedAt` because the generic schema scaffold uses the same trailing system columns for all tables. This differs from the requested future rule of avoiding delete fields on audit/log tables.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### AppSheet consumer scan) Tj
T*
(- No direct AppSheet integration, AppConfig, webhook handler, `_Key` formula column, read-only AppSheet annotations, or formula-column comments were found.) Tj
T*
(- Therefore no table can be positively flagged as AppSheet-consumed from current code.) Tj
T*
() Tj
